  "caption": "AMOC evolution and hysteresis pathways at the native latitude nearest26.5N. Panel a shows nine-model initial-decade anomalies, the equal-weight mean and intermodel population SD, with prescribed CO2 on a separate right axis. Panels b,d,f are idealized schematics of recovery with small A, recovery with large A, and non-recovery. Only panel d labels the shaded hysteresis area A, with an arrow from its blank lower portion; panel f retains open-path shading without an area label. The small-A schematic shows gently curved, separated branches enclosing a narrow closed area. Panels c,e,g overlay2,3,4actual model trajectories, respectively. Each model keeps its panel-a color for its complete CO2 rise-and-fall trajectory; all paths are solid and arrows show time direction. Actual trajectories remain the saved26.5N11yr centred means normalized by each model's raw years1-10 strength. No actual endpoint is forced to close and no actual small nonzero area is replaced by zero; the group names are descriptive author labels. Schematics are conceptual rather than fitted model curves or equilibrium branches. Parentheses in the panel-a legend give mean AMOC strength over experiment years1-10 in Sv at the same native latitude; the9-model mean is the equal-weight average of those means.",
